<span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Start by letting the chicken slices marinate while prepping the veggies. Then start heating up the pan. As soon as the pan is hot you can start frying the chicken in two batches. It only takes about 3 minutes per batch. Don&#39;t crowd the pan because you don&#39;t want the chicken to steam or worse yet boil. Leaving space between the slices will allow the liquids to evaporate more rapidly.</span></h5>\n\n<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\">&nbsp;</h5>\n\n<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Remove the chicken to a plate or bowl while you stir-fry the veggies.&nbsp;</span></h5>\n\n<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></h5>\n\n<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Add the curry paste and the chicken&nbsp;to the veggies when they are just barely tender, then add the coconut milk and bring the whole thing to a boil for just a minute to warm everything through and it&#39;s time to eat!</span></h5>\n\n<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></h5>\n\n<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Click through the images below for a better look.</span></h5>","skin":"WRichTex